Dispatch assigns apparatus by call type. The assignments below are the default — command can request more at any time.

## Assignments

| Call type | Default response |
| --------- | ---------------- |
| Structure fire | Two engines, one ladder, one medic, battalion chief |
| Vehicle fire | One engine |
| Motor vehicle collision | One engine, one rescue, one medic |
| Medical call | One medic |
| Alarm activation | One engine |
| Brush or outdoor fire | One engine, one tanker |

<Warning>
A reported entrapment, a report of people trapped inside, or any working fire upgrades the response immediately. Do not wait for arrival to confirm — start the extra apparatus and cancel them later if not needed.
</Warning>

## On arrival

<Steps>

<Step title="Give a size-up">
First unit on scene reports what it sees: building type, what is showing, and whether anyone is reported inside. Everyone still responding is listening to this.
</Step>

<Step title="Establish command">
State who has command and where. "Engine One has command, Alpha side."
</Step>

<Step title="Assign incoming units">
Give each arriving apparatus a task before it arrives. Unassigned crews create freelancing.
</Step>

<Step title="Account for personnel">
Track who is inside and where. Run a headcount at every change in strategy.
</Step>

<Step title="Terminate and report">
Announce the scene is clear, return units to available, and file the incident report before signing off.
</Step>

</Steps>

## Scene coordination with OPP

<AccordionGroup>

<Accordion title="Traffic and perimeter belong to police" icon="triangle-alert">
Request a block rather than setting one yourself. Apparatus positioning for protection is fire's call; road closure is not.
</Accordion>

<Accordion title="Fire scenes that become investigations" icon="clipboard-list">
Where a fire is suspicious, preserve the scene and hand it to police. Limit overhaul to what safety requires.
</Accordion>

<Accordion title="One channel for the incident" icon="radio">
Command talks to dispatch. Individual crews talk to command, not directly to police units on another channel.
</Accordion>

</AccordionGroup>

<Note>
Response assignments are a template and should match whatever your department actually runs.
</Note>
